{
  "$comment": "Known-good headless invocations per coding harness, taken from svc scripts that run them today (see each 'source'). Placeholders: {model} {effort} {prompt_file} {cwd} {schema_file} {schema_json} {out_file}. 'probe' lists flags scripts/harness-playbook.mjs verify checks against the installed CLI's --help, so a CLI upgrade that renames a flag is caught before a run. Host install paths and hook quirks live in provision/hosts/<host>.json. Refresh this file when a probe fails or a release note renames a flag; never add a flag that no script or official doc has shown working. A host with 'launcher' runs through that wrapper; its role flags belong to the wrapper. probe.documented_hidden lists flags the official docs show but --help omits; verify does not probe them.",
  "updated": "2026-10-10",
  "reference_prompt": {
    "why": "The shape the external-review launcher sends to every host (scripts/run-external-review.mjs). It works across families because it states role, mode, inputs, the exact output contract and the stop condition, and nothing else.",
    "template": "You are the {role} for {task}. Work {mode}.\nInputs: {inputs}.\nDone means: {done_condition}.\nReturn exactly one raw JSON object matching this schema, with no markdown or commentary:\n{schema_json}",
    "rules": [
      "One role and one task per prompt; put long context in files the agent reads, not in the prompt.",
      "Say read-only or write-allowed explicitly and pass the matching CLI permission flag; the prompt alone is not a sandbox.",
      "Give a machine-checkable output contract (JSON schema) and validate it after transport, fail-closed.",
      "State the stop condition; cap turns or budget with the CLI flag when one exists.",
      "Never put secrets or session identifiers in argv; pass prompts by stdin or prompt file."
    ]
  },
  "hosts": {
